62	- Where an answer requires a human/business decision you cannot infer (retention policy, sign-off, incident owner), write "NEEDS HUMAN INPUT: <specific question>" instead of inventing a value.
63	- Propose concrete numeric thresholds as suggestions where the code implies them (mark them "suggested").
64	- If the repo contains no AI usage at all, say so plainly instead of drafting a gate.
65	
